A||N||14||Ferrari355||VERY BAD AND UPSETTING fiero day for me!!!||||8||
Z||000000||Ferrari355||02-25-2000||07:45 PM||||Well, i am so phucking pissed off at my parents. Ok well the Fiero GT i was so excited about, we aren't getting. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> My dad decided that he wasn't going to get it for some reason. Have no clue why. I mean, my dad like begged my mom to get the loan and she said no until he lowered the price, and when he finnally lower the price, we got the loan.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">But nnnnnoooooo, we have to back down one day before we get it. I was all excited, and was real happy at school today casue i figured he would go get it tomorrow. But when i heard the trajic words, i was so pissed. This may sound funny but i was so pissed i cried. And that is majorly pissed. Well, the guy said if we don't buy it he will keep it so it will atleast be in good hands. There is sorta some good news. I am going to get our '89 Trans Am, but i wanted the fiero cause they are so awesome, they aren't like anything out there, they are so individual. Well that is all i have to say. I will still come here everyday. And just basicly dream......until i'm 16, i guess i won't have a GT. so sad..bye  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000001||Phil||02-25-2000||08:09 PM||||A 16 year old should be thanking his parents on bended knee for any kind of car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||02-25-2000||08:29 PM||||Phil, sounds like its been a looooooooooooooooong time since you were 14 and had your heart set on something that you thought was really cool. I wouldn't expect you to understand.<BR>Alex, take a breath buddy. Let me tell you somethin about haggling. If the guy is ready to drop a grand off of his asking price, who knows what kind of attitude readjust he can go through in a week or 2. Give the folks a break. You still have 1 Fiero in the house to play with and 2 years before you can drive. Ease up!<BR> A little aside... I cannot tell you how many really cool cars my dad bought that I set my sights on "buying someday"... Pantera, Scirooco GTI eurospec, even the LeBaron convertible with the dope white leather interior.  All sold before I had my chance.  When I bought my GT, I really knew it was MINE! Felt better than coveting the old mans wheels, believe me.<BR>My advice, keep on learning everything you can about the car and start saving that birthday and christmas money. By the time you hit 16 you can start negotiating for your own plasticmobile. There will still be some around for you.  <BR>Take it easy kid! ||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||02-25-2000||08:41 PM||||Sorry you didn't get that GT, Ferrari.  But an 89 T/A is still pretty nice!  And at least it's a Pontiac.||||reg||9
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||02-25-2000||08:43 PM||||Alex, Stimpy is right, Hang tight your Fiero will come. You sound like a smart young man and you know what you want. Let me tell you there are some really cool stuff that I would like to buy for my fiero but the wife says NO and when she says NO it means NO, but when I think about it some times shes right, it cost too much at the time. And when I wait mmost times something better/cheaper comes along. Don't get me wrong I wear the pants in this house....., but she tells me which ones  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">  Stay with us Alex and learn about this little plastic thing and soon you'll have one bad ride!! And thats fo sho!<P>Peace<BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
Z||000005||wkayl||02-25-2000||08:47 PM||||My Dad bought me my 1st car.  It was a 1953 Ford Mainline 4 door for $23.  He had to buy a wrecked car so I could get enough parts to get it to pass MV Inspection.  My son turned 16 in July of '98.  He had ben saving his money (from birthdays, Christmas and yes babysitting)for about 3 years and had about $800 saved up.  We went looking for a Fiero after he turned 16 and found an 84SE for $1,100.  He got a job and paid us back the amount we had to advance him.  So keep your head up and wait it out.  You can do it too.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||02-25-2000||09:03 PM||||Hey Alex, DXR_DAD has been keeping me pretty informed of your ordeal.  I really feel for you right now, but what I want to say is, if you parents feel that this isn't working for them, rest assured, it probably is a well thought out decision.  Although I know that this doesn't make you feel any better.  Like I tell DXR_DAD, hold off, there has to either be a better deal somewhere else, or if this is they only good deal around, then it will resurfacee again and maybe, that what's happening here.  Hang on to your dreams. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>DXR_MOM||||reg||7
Z||000007||Ferrari355||02-25-2000||09:55 PM||||Thanks everyone, i'm alittle better now, i was jsut pissed. I was so frustrated. I guess i'll have to start liking the TA again. I still like it though. I think this forum needs to have an annaul drawing to win a 87 Fiero GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> But, I WILL eventually get a Fiero GT! i will earn enough money sometime somewhere. Well anyway, i better go... Thanks for your support of my stage of major drepression. HEHE Bye...||||reg||7
Z||000008||fierospeeder||02-25-2000||10:21 PM||||Im into vw bugs the old ones, and fieros.  But i was more into the bugs.  My mom saw this awesome bug, 71 super beetle that was red.  Everything was perfect and the guy brought it from arizona or one of those warm states.  He wanted 5000 i think and we talked to the guy for an hour about beetles.  I think we were going to get it for 3500.  But few days later when we were going to have this vw bug mechanic look over it, my mom backed out.  But she did buy me a fiero few months later.<P>My dad is the worst, he doesn't buy me a lot of things, or any.  He doesn't know anything about cars, and i have to fix his car if he tells me 50 times.  About few years ago, my mom was into housesales and i wouldn't go because its so lame going to those.  One time she came home and told me there was a motorbike for sale for 300 bucks. DROOL, i always wanted a bike and i have driven them before on my grandparents farm (on my moms side) when i was 11.  I went back to that housesale, and it was like a 80cc yamaha and it came with a helmet and chest protection.  I begged my mom to buy it and my dad said he didn't want to get it.  <BR>Only if my dad was more redneck i might be driving an ATV.  damit||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||02-25-2000||11:10 PM||||DXR_PARENTS--Well said.  DAD, it's the same in my house.  It makes me mad sometimes when Monkeygirl tells me what I can and can't buy, but when I look back on it, it's usually (OK.  Always.) the right decision.  If I had my way, I'd have tons of parts for my Fiero but no house to park in front of.<BR>Excerpt from a song by Rodney Carrington (I think):  "I wear the pants in this house...when I get done with the laundry.  I can watch sports anytime I want...to sleep on the couch.  I can have *** any time...you want to."  (Etc, etc)||||reg||1
Z||000010||Shiner||02-26-2000||12:57 AM||||Too bad about the GT F355 ;(  My first car, which was also my first fiero, was an '84 SC, which I busted my rump for at the local video store.  I still have her, sitting in the yard with a couple of problems.  I got my '87 GT about 2 years after that, and I am currently restoring it.  So I HAVE an '87 GT and I can't even drive it!!!  Maybe this car just wasn't meant to be!  I almost bought a gorgeous '86 SE 2m6 before I got my GT.  The car was PERFECT on the interior, and had a gorgeous red paint job.  It ran terrific too.  I almost bought it, but it just didn't seem right.  You will find the right car some day man.  Just wait it out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
